{
  "id": "added-dependency-benign-library",
  "title": "A benign new dependency does not make the release high risk",
  "category": "dependency-introduction",
  "intent": "The hard negative for dependency review. A release adds an ordinary HTTP helper: it has a network capability, but nothing runs on install, so the release must not be graded risky merely because a dependency is new. Adding dependencies is normal software work.",
  "previousPackageJson": { "name": "app-lib", "version": "2.0.0", "main": "index.js" },
